INT. ABANDONED OBSERVATORY - DOME ROOM - NIGHT

A round chamber under a split copper dome. A huge brass telescope aimed at a hole in the roof where stars blink through. Dust like snow. Star charts curl on the walls.

DR. HELENA VASQUEZ-MURRAY, 50s, trench coat over pajamas, mud on her boots, kneels by the telescope's base with a flashlight clenched in her teeth. She runs her fingers along the floor. Pulls up a loose board. Beneath it, a leather journal wrapped in oilcloth.

HELENA
(muffled by the flashlight)
There you are.

She takes the flashlight from her mouth. Unwraps the journal. Opens it to the first page. Reads in a whisper.

HELENA (CONT'D)
"If you are reading this, I have already gone to see what the telescope shows after midnight."

She turns a page. A hand-drawn sketch of the sky. Beside one star, a small red circle and the word NO.

HELENA (CONT'D)
No what?

Her phone buzzes in her pocket. She answers.

DETECTIVE GRANT (V.O.)
(over the phone)
Helena, where are you?

HELENA
Following the lead.

DETECTIVE GRANT (V.O.)
At the observatory? I told you to wait for backup.

HELENA
Backup is slow. The journal is here.

DETECTIVE GRANT (V.O.)
Don't touch anything. We think Warrick didn't die alone.

HELENA
(shining the light across the floor)
I'm not alone either.

Footprints in the dust. Not hers. Wide, deliberate. They lead to the stairwell.

DETECTIVE GRANT (V.O.)
Helena, did you hear me?

HELENA
Stay on the line.

She lays the phone on the telescope base. Rises. Follows the footprints with the light. They end at a door in the wall. Half open. A sliver of darkness behind it.

A shape fills the gap. A TALL MAN in a gray overcoat, face hidden by a brimmed hat, steps into the dome. Slow. Unhurried. In one gloved hand he holds a brass key.

TALL MAN
You found it before I did.

HELENA
(steady)
You're Warrick's partner.

TALL MAN
I was his student.

HELENA
Did you kill him?

TALL MAN
(a pause)
I closed the shutter. He opened it.

Helena raises the journal. The Tall Man's eyes follow it.

HELENA
Then tell me what the star is.

TALL MAN
You already know.

HELENA
Say it.

DETECTIVE GRANT (V.O.)
(tinny, from the telescope)
Helena! Who are you talking to?

The Tall Man glances at the phone. Then back at her. He lifts the key. Behind him, the dome's great shutter groans and begins to close, cutting the stars off one slice at a time.

HELENA
(shouting)
Grant! Now!

She hurls the journal across the floor. The Tall Man lunges for it. The dome slams shut. Darkness. A single crack of flashlight on the floor.

Sirens, very far away.
